From: VultaV <unc10@naver.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: succeed when deleting an absent host FDB entry

The local mac80211 station teardown notifier can request deletion after
the bridge has already aged or moved an address, or before it was learned.
Each bridged DSA user port forwards that notification to the CPU port.
An absent entry in the CPU port's reference-counted FDB list then returns
-ENOENT, filling the log with one error per user port and station teardown.
The mt7530 port_fdb_del operation is not reached in this case.

The requested end state is already satisfied. Keep the not-found trace
event but return success, as for a reference-count decrement. Leave driver
errors and deletion of existing entries unchanged. This also preserves
the station notifier's immediate bridge flow cleanup.

Signed-off-by: VultaV <unc10@naver.com>
---
 net/dsa/switch.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

--- a/net/dsa/switch.c
+++ b/net/dsa/switch.c
@@ -326,7 +326,6 @@ static int dsa_port_do_fdb_del(struct dsa_port *dp, const unsigned char *addr,
 	a = dsa_mac_addr_find(&dp->fdbs, addr, vid, db);
 	if (!a) {
 		trace_dsa_fdb_del_not_found(dp, addr, vid, &db);
-		err = -ENOENT;
 		goto out;
 	}
 
